I know *exactly* why it feels stuck! This is a classic Material-UI (MUI) lifecycle trap.
Here is the culprit:
You had this line in both Autocompletes:
onClose={() => setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: "" }))}
**Here is what was happening:** 1. You search and find "Branch A".
2. You click "Branch A".
3. The backend successfully selects "Branch A" and saves it.
4. The dropdown closes -> triggering onClose.
5. onClose instantly overwrites the text box with "" (blank)!
Because it blanked out instantly, it looked to you like the selection failed or got "stuck", when in reality, the UI was just deleting the text right before your eyes!
To fix this, we need to completely delete the manual open and onClose overrides and let MUI naturally handle the open/close state.
Here are the precise replacements for both Autocomplete components.
### 1. Fix the Branch Autocomplete
Find your Branch <Autocomplete> (around line 527) and replace it with this. Notice we have completely removed open={...} and onClose={...}:
```javascript
                  <Autocomplete
                    // LET MUI HANDLE OPEN/CLOSE AUTOMATICALLY
                    popupIcon={null}
                    autoHighlight
                    options={branchSearch.options}
                    getOptionLabel={(option) => option && option.code ? `${option.code} - ${option.name}` : ""}
                    value={row.branch || null}
                    onChange={(event, newValue) => handleRowChange(row.id, "branch", newValue)}
                    inputValue={branchInputValues[row.id] || ""}
                    onInputChange={(event, newInputValue, reason) => {
                      if (reason === 'input') {
                        const cleanInput = filterAndWarn(newInputValue, "alphanumeric_space");
                        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: cleanInput }));
                        searchBranches(cleanInput, row.id);
                      } else {
                        // This safely handles when the user clicks an option or clicks away
                        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: newInputValue }));
                      }
                    }}
                    loading={branchSearch.loadingId === row.id}
                    filterOptions={(x) => x}
                    isOptionEqualToValue={(option, value) => option?.code === value?.code}
                    noOptionsText={
                      (branchInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3 
                        ? "Type at least 3 characters..." 
                        : "Branch not found"
                    }
                    renderInput={(params) => (
                      <Tooltip title="Search by Branch name or Branch code" placement="top-start">
                        <TextField
                          {...params}
                          label="Branch *"
                          placeholder="Type to search..."
                          InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }}
                          InputProps={{
                            ...params.InputProps,
                            endAdornment: (
                              <Box>
                                {branchSearch.loadingId === row.id ? (
                                  <CircularProgress color="inherit" size={20} />
                                ) : null}
                                {params.InputProps.endAdornment}
                              </Box>
                            ),
                          }}
                        />
                      </Tooltip>
                    )}
                  />

```
### 2. Fix the CGL Autocomplete
Find your CGL <Autocomplete> (around line 656) and apply the exact same fix by replacing it with this:
```javascript
                  <Autocomplete
                    // LET MUI HANDLE OPEN/CLOSE AUTOMATICALLY
                    popupIcon={null}
                    autoHighlight
                    options={cglSearch.options}
                    getOptionLabel={(option) => option && option.cglNumber ? `${option.cglNumber} - ${option.description}` : ""}
                    value={row.cgl || null}
                    onChange={(event, newValue) => handleRowChange(row.id, "cgl", newValue)}
                    inputValue={cglInputValues[row.id] || ""}
                    onInputChange={(event, newInputValue, reason) => {
                      if (reason === 'input') {
                        const cleanInput = filterAndWarn(newInputValue, "alphanumeric_space");
                        setCglInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: cleanInput }));
                        searchCgls(cleanInput, row.id);
                      } else {
                        // This safely handles when the user clicks an option or clicks away
                        setCglInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: newInputValue }));
                      }
                    }}
                    loading={cglSearch.loadingId === row.id}
                    filterOptions={(x) => x}
                    isOptionEqualToValue={(option, value) => option?.cglNumber === value?.cglNumber}
                    noOptionsText={
                      (cglInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3 
                        ? "Type at least 3 characters..." 
                        : "CGL not found"
                    }
                    renderInput={(params) => (
                      <Tooltip title="Search by CGL or CGL Description" placement="top-start">
                        <TextField
                          {...params}
                          label="CGL *"
                          placeholder="Type to search..."
                          InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }}
                          InputProps={{
                            ...params.InputProps,
                            endAdornment: (
                              <Box sx={{ marginLeft: "2%", display: "flex", alignItems: "center" }}>
                                {row.cgl && String(row.cgl.cglNumber).startsWith("5") && (
                                  <Chip label="MEMO" size="small" color="warning" sx={{ height: 20, fontSize: "0.7rem", mr: 1 }} />
                                )}
                                {cglSearch.loadingId === row.id ? <CircularProgress color="inherit" size={20} /> : null}
                                {params.InputProps.endAdornment}
                              </Box>
                            ),
                          }}
                        />
                      </Tooltip>
                    )}
                  />

```
Now, when you click on the dropdown option, the onClose function won't aggressively delete the text! The option label (e.g., 1234 - Cash Account) will perfectly lock into the input box exactly as you expect. Try it out!
